body:
[A10] Owner decision, 2026-10-01: the end station must be able to follow either an AAF talker's media clock or a CRF talker's media clock, with exactly one source selected at a time through its CLOCK_DOMAIN. This reverses #389 option (a) (2026-09-09) for AAF listeners. The CRF path stays.

## Double check first: spec and implementation

- **Milan v1.2 5.3.3.6** (the CLOCK_SOURCE set of a CLOCK_DOMAIN):
  - the repository currently reads it as one INPUT_STREAM source per CRF input, or the single AAF input when no CRF input exists;
  - confirm it against the clause text, and record whether an INPUT_STREAM source per AAF Stream Input may sit beside the CRF source.
- **Milan v1.2:**
  - 7.2.2 (the CRF Media Clock Input);
  - 7.4 (source quality, ±50 ppm);
  - 5.4.2.15 and 5.4.2.16 (SET/GET_CLOCK_SOURCE; an unlisted index gets BAD_ARGUMENTS);
  - 5.3.11.1 (the selected source is saved state).
- **IEEE 1722.1-2021:** 7.2.9 (CLOCK_SOURCE), 7.2.32 (CLOCK_DOMAIN) and 7.4.23.1 (SET_CLOCK_SOURCE).
- **IEEE 1722-2016 §4.4.4.3:** `mr` when the followed stream is disrupted. It applies to AAF and CRF following alike.
- **The current state:**
  - the shipping configs declare `media_clock_sources: [internal, crf]`;
  - FR-CLK-03 and FR-CLK-04 (`docs/reference/FR_NFR.md`) and the builder refuse `input_stream` since #389.

## Work

- [ ] **Requirements:** amend FR-CLK-03, FR-CLK-04 and the #389 record to this decision.
- [ ] **Model and builder:**
  - add an INPUT_STREAM CLOCK_SOURCE per AAF Stream Input, located on that input, beside INTERNAL and the CRF source;
  - the CLOCK_DOMAIN lists them all;
  - exactly one is selected.
- [ ] **Fabric:**
  - recover the media clock from the selected AAF stream's presentation timestamps, through the same servo path the CRF source drives;
  - gate it on the live selection;
  - a source switch re-locks without an undeclared discontinuity.
- [ ] **Lock loss of the selected stream (AAF or CRF):** the declared holdover and restart behaviour, and `mr` per IEEE 1722-2016 §4.4.4.3.
- [ ] **Protocol processor:** SET/GET_CLOCK_SOURCE over the longer source list, and the selection kept as saved state.

## Proof and acceptance

- [ ] **Simulation:**
  - each source (INTERNAL, AAF, CRF) selected in turn;
  - the media clock follows the selected talker's rate offset within tolerance;
  - switching and lock loss each graded by a failing mutant.
- [ ] **Bench, both directions, each followed source:**
  - the listener's CLOCK_DOMAIN is set by SET_CLOCK_SOURCE to the followed stream and read back;
  - the listener's format is adapted before every bind, never the talker's;
  - the as-found source is restored at teardown.
- [ ] **Bench quality metric:** the THD+N and SNR of a known tone on the selected path, graded against two controls:
  - the listener left on INTERNAL, where the metric must show the mismatch;
  - slips and drift planted in a synthetic capture.

Relates to #74 (CRF selection and grid alignment), #389, #117 and #386.
